## Evidence

Open work migrated from the canonical TODO. Add implementation and
validation evidence here as the task advances.

A persistent September 5 port-preview transaction now proves that reviewed
source-backed artifacts can cross the live native MCP boundary without waiting
for the incomplete global plan. `l1z1`, Cletus, and `sedana` were imported under
`/Game/Generated/SHAR/PortPreview`; the resulting Static Mesh, two Skeletal
Meshes, and two Skeleton companions were explicitly saved and independently
read back as clean packages. Three unsaved preview actors were then placed in
the currently loaded open-world editor map and focused in the viewport. Those
actor transforms are inspection-only and are deliberately not saved as world
assembly authority.

The global executor remains fail-closed. Its accepted bundle still contains
34,156 ready direct imports plus 52 editor-factory operations alongside 957
semantic blockers, so no partial subset is reported as the complete plan. The
dedicated vehicle catalog is now entering `prepare-unreal` through a separate
read-only verification boundary rather than through an ignore-blockers switch.
